<h2 id="choose-requirements-by-institutional-responsibility">Choose requirements by institutional responsibility</h2>

<p>For a <strong>university</strong>, the registrar owns authoritative award records, academic teams approve assessment meaning, IT verifies interfaces and privacy, and career services reviews market interpretation. For a <strong>certification body</strong>, expiry, renewal and authority to award matter. For <strong>L&amp;D</strong>, account provisioning, recurring learning rules and integration failures matter. For a <strong>training provider</strong>, reliable delivery, recipient experience and controlled award criteria matter.</p>

<p>None of these use cases is a sufficient reason to declare a vendor universally best. Ask each shortlisted vendor to demonstrate the same authorized sample and exception cases.</p>

<h2 id="procurement-questions-to-ask">Procurement questions to ask</h2>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Standards:</strong> which exact format, version, proof and certified role apply to the product being offered? Check the current <a href="https://site.imsglobal.org/certifications">1EdTech registry</a>. Support and certification are distinct; certification is not a privacy/security audit.</li>
  <li><strong>Lifecycle:</strong> how are corrections, renewals, expiration and revocation represented? What happens when a status endpoint is unavailable or cached?</li>
  <li><strong>Integration:</strong> which connector, API permission and plan handle the actual SIS/LMS/HRIS event? Test retries, duplicates, failed delivery and account removal.</li>
  <li><strong>Security:</strong> request current scoped audit documentation and applicable ISO certificates, with dates, exceptions, legal entity and hosting region. GDPR obligations are not a generic product certificate.</li>
  <li><strong>Pricing:</strong> compare recipient and issuance limits, renewals, API access, domains, support, administrators and export—not only a headline per-credential cost.</li>
  <li><strong>Continuity:</strong> what data and proof can be exported, and who maintains issuer keys, status and evidence resources after termination? Standards reduce some lock-in but do not guarantee issuer-independent verification forever.</li>
  <li><strong>Career context:</strong> what is sourced market data versus an inferred skill match or measured employment outcome?</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="workforce-data-is-not-graduate-outcome-evidence">Workforce data is not graduate-outcome evidence</h2>

<p>Credly describes external occupation insights and 24/7 job-posting updates. CertifyMe’s own job-farming engine covers 20 million live jobs from 50,000 companies worldwide, refreshed every two weeks. These first-party statements describe different datasets and update processes, not independently comparable benchmarks. Test relevance, freshness and geographic coverage against the same programme. A job match or salary band does not show that a learner obtained employment.</p>

